  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong>Chromosomal Abnormality</strong></span></th>\n<th><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong>Gene/Fusion Detected</strong></span></th>\n<th><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong>Associated with</strong></span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">t(8;21)(q22;q22)</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">RUNX1-RUNX1T1 (AML1-ETO)</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">AML with maturation</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">inv(16)(p13q22) / t(16;16)</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">CBFB-MYH11</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">AML with eosinophilia</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">t(15;17)(q24;q21)</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">PML-RARA</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Acute promyelocytic leukemia (APL)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">11q23 rearrangements</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">MLL/KMT2A</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Monocytic AML, poor prognosis</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">del(5q), del(7q), +8</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Various cytogenetic markers</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Myelodysplastic changes, poor prognosis</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1731\" data-end=\"2021\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1731\" data-end=\"1884\">\n<p data-start=\"1733\" data-end=\"1884\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1733\" data-end=\"1745\">Abnormal</strong>: Suggests presence of genetic translocations or deletions commonly found in <strong data-start=\"1822\" data-end=\"1829\">AML</strong>; helps guide <strong data-start=\"1843\" data-end=\"1856\">prognosis</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1861\" data-end=\"1883\">treatment strategy</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1885\" data-end=\"2021\">\n<p data-start=\"1887\" data-end=\"2021\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1887\" data-end=\"1897\">Normal</strong>: No detectable chromosomal abnormalities in the tested panel. Does not rule out AML; molecular testing may still be needed.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote data-start=\"2023\" data-end=\"2153\">\n<p data-start=\"2025\" data-end=\"2153\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"2025\" data-end=\"2034\">Note:</strong> FISH is a targeted test and complements <strong data-start=\"2075\" data-end=\"2090\">karyotyping</strong> and <strong data-start=\"2095\" data-end=\"2152\">molecular mutation analysis (e.g., FLT3, NPM1, CEBPA)</strong>.</span></p>\n</blockquote>",
